<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Miguel Primo de Rivera</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1870–1930</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Miguel Primo de Rivera was a Spanish general who seized power in a coup in September 1923 and ruled as dictator with the backing of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-xiii">Alfonso XIII</a> until January 1930. His regime ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rif-war">Rif War</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> with French help and invested in public works, but lost support amid economic trouble. His fall helped bring down the monarchy in 1931.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/miguel-primo-de-rivera.jpg" alt="Miguel Primo de Rivera" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kaulak · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Miguel_Primo_de_Rivera,_Kaulak_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
